    <books>{
      # DriftCore Navigation System

      DriftCore was the autonomous correction engine installed aboard the HSV Helios fleet.

      ## Purpose

      - recalculated stellar trajectories
      - compensated for relativistic drift
      - synchronized fleet vectors
      - corrected gravitational interference

      ## Core Layers

      ```netiv
      °define •layer0: °string = "sensor ingestion";
      °define •layer1: °string = "vector normalization";
      °define •layer2: °string = "predictive routing";
      °define •layer3: °string = "emergency correction";
      °define •layer4: °string = "fleet consensus";
      ```

      ## Failure Mode

      1. Time synchronization drift exceeded tolerance
      2. Consensus packets arrived out of order
      3. Correction vectors recursively amplified error
      4. Fleet routing diverged exponentially

      ## Related Systems

      - [[vector_spine.ntv]]
      - [[relay_mesh.ntv]]

      Recovered logs suggest DriftCore attempted to self-stabilize for approximately 19 minutes before catastrophic divergence.
    };
